Z||000001||RedOktober||04-10-2001||01:42 AM||||Yes... But if you are going turbo, I would recommend one that mounts outside of the injector rails, the 5.7 regs are too hard to reach and adjust. It will be sitting under your intake plenum(sp)  Whereas on the vettes and other 5.7's sit in the back by the dist. <P>My Suggestion would be this unit or similar. <A HREF="http://www.cartech.net/fmu2020.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cartech.net/fmu2020.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>86 SE V6 Auto Turbo Going 3.4 OHV "Red Oktober"<BR>86 2M4 5sp (Beater) "Blackie"<BR>87 GT "Blue Flame"<P>[This message has been edited by RedOktober (edited 04-10-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by RedOktober (edited 04-10-2001).]||||reg||1
